## Critical Observations & Issues Identified

### 1. Active Git Merge State - RESOLVED
The previously stuck merge state (`MERGE_HEAD = 0611a26`) has been fully resolved and committed (`14af52c5`):
* Removed conflict markers (`<<<<<<< HEAD` / `=======` / `>>>>>>>`) from all 14 affected XML profile files in `Default Profiles/GatherBuddy2/` (which contained duplicate identical copies).
* Cleaned up 27 obsolete/missing file paths (`Default Profiles/Herbs/` and old `SimpleGrindZone.csproj` that were renamed/reorganized).
* Staged all 886 conflict-free added files and all modernized bot improvements ([Tyrael](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Tyrael), [Templar](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar), [AutoAngler2](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2)).
* Concluded merge with zero unresolved conflicts remaining.

### 2. Runtime Exceptions in Logs (`Logs/Helios - Buttermilk/` & `Mendermike`) - RESOLVED
* **OnBotChanged NullReferenceException** (`0747fc8f`):
  `FuryUnleashed.Core.Helpers.BotEvents.OnBotChanged(EventArgs args)` and `GladiatorSuite` / `PureRotation` / `Oracle` handlers crashed when bot instances changed while `BotManager.Current` or internal routine state was null. Guarded across all affected routines.
* **AutoAngler / FishingBuddy vs. AutoEquip Conflict** (`AutoAngler.cs`, `FishingBuddy.cs`):
  Suppressed `CharacterSettings.Instance.AutoEquipWeapons` and loaded `AutoEquip` plugins while fishing, restoring state on `Stop()`.
* **Dead Updater / Auth / Telemetry Calls** (`64ddc4e9`, `5b8c3787`, `ff893a21`, `9887e515` .. `f63a54be`):
  Neutralized defunct HTTP/SVN/TLS update checks, remote auth gates, and StatCounter/analytics calls across core `Honorbuddy.exe`, bots, and all combat routines.
* **HB Core `FlightPaths.smethod_0` & Navigation Crashes** (`a755d6dc`):
  Diagnosed and fixed `InvalidOperationException: Sequence contains no matching element` in `Styx.CommonBot.FlightPaths` by sanitizing polluted `<Connections />` DBC nodes out of `FlightPaths.XmlNodes` and `FlightPaths.xml` without wrapping/disposing `MeshNavigator`.

