## Bot Modernization & Fix Status

### 1. Tyrael (`Bots/Tyrael/`) - Completed & In-Game Verified
* **Target Framework**: Updated from legacy v4.0 to strict `.NET Framework 4.5.1` (x86).
* **Reference Paths**: Resolved assembly paths pointing to root directory `..\..\Honorbuddy.exe` and added required `WindowsBase` reference.
* **Dead SVN Updater**: Replaced unreachable Assembla SVN check in `TyraelUpdater.cs` with safe local revision reporting (`Revision 5.6.4`).
* **Dead Telemetry**: Removed external StatCounter network ping in `TyraelUtilities.cs`.
* **Behavior Tree Null-Safety**: Reconstructed `CreateRoot()` in `Tyrael.cs` to guard null references in `HealBehavior`, `CombatBuffBehavior`, `RestBehavior`, and `PreCombatBuffBehavior`.
* **Root Invalidation**: Added `BotEvents.Player.OnMapChanged` and `Stop()` invalidation (`_root = null`).
* **Status**: **Verified Working in WoW MoP 5.4.8**.

### 2. Templar (`Bots/Templar/`) - Completed & Compiled Cleanly
* **Behavior Tree Null-Safety & Guards ([Composites.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/Composites.cs))**:
  - Dynamically builds children for `PreCombatRoutine`, `PullRoutine`, and `CombatRoutine` with null checks for `RoutineManager.Current` and its behaviors.
  - Guarded `RestBehavior` with `RoutineManager.Current.NeedRest` and `PreCombatBuffBehavior` with `RoutineManager.Current.NeedPreCombatBuffs`.
  - Added death/ghost guard `!StyxWoW.Me.IsDead && !StyxWoW.Me.IsGhost` across pre-combat and combat trees so death logic takes full precedence.
* **Flight & Dismounting Logic ([PriorityTreeState.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/PriorityTreeState.cs))**:
  - Removed `|| Variables.NextMob != null` from the top-level emergency dismount check (which was causing the bot to immediately dismount mid-air 100 yards away when a mob was spotted or when returning to start location).
  - Kept emergency dismount strictly for unexpected combat (`StyxWoW.Me.Combat || Variables.MobsTargettingMe > 0`).
  - Removed redundant transition dismount in `ReadyForTask` so the bot can fly/navigate into pull range before dismounting.
  - Fixed `_pullStartTime` bleed-through across mobs and ensured it resets on combat, on target death/loss, and after completing `MoveToTarget`.
* **Disenchanting Bug ([Disenchant.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/Disenchant.cs))**:
  - Fixed logic bug where `ProtectedItemSettings.Instance.ProtectedItems.All(pi => pi.Entry == i.Entry)` was used. (In LINQ, `.All(...)` on an empty collection returns `true`, causing every item in the game to be marked "protected" when no protected items were configured). Changed to `.Any(pi => pi.Entry == i.Entry)`.
* **Lifecycle & Root Caching ([Templar.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Templar.cs))**:
  - Added `Initialize()` with `BotEvents.Player.OnMapChanged` to invalidate `_root = null` on map changes.
  - Invalidate `_root = null` on `Start()` and `Stop()`.
* **Blacklist & Diagnostics ([CustomBlacklist.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/CustomBlacklist.cs), [CustomLog.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/CustomLog.cs))**:
  - Added null guard for `_sweepTimer` in `RemoveExpired()`.
  - Added `ClearAll()` and invoked on bot `Stop()`.
  - Fixed array value comparison in `CustomLog.cs` to eliminate repetitive console spamming while preserving diagnostic logging.
* **Pull Distance & Log Explosion Fix ([TaskManager.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/TaskManager.cs), [Variables.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/Variables.cs), [PriorityTreeState.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/Templar/Helpers/PriorityTreeState.cs))**:
  - Replaced hardcoded `> 50` yard cutoff in `TaskManager.HandlePulling()` with dynamic `Variables.EffectivePullDistance` (5 yds for melee, 25 yds for ranged). Previously, Templar stopped moving at 50 yards and froze for 7 seconds because 40-yard spells could not reach.
  - Eliminated rapid-fire log explosion in `MoveToTarget` by centralizing state-change logging and throttling distance logs with a 3-second timer.
  - Immediately cancel `MoveToTarget` and halt movement if the player begins casting (`IsCasting || IsChanneling`), preventing interrupted pull spell casts.
* **Compilation Status**: Verified 0 errors with Microsoft C# 5.0 compiler targeting .NET 4.5.1 x86.

### 3. AutoAngler2 (`Bots/AutoAngler2/`) - Completed & Compiled Cleanly
* **Project Modernization ([AutoAngler2.csproj](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/AutoAngler2.csproj))**:
  - Upgraded target framework from legacy v4.0 to `.NET Framework 4.5.1` (x86).
  - Fixed relative HintPaths for `GreyMagic.dll`, `Honorbuddy.exe`, and `Tripper.Tools.dll`.
  - Removed failing `PreBuildEvent` (`SubWCRev.exe`) which broke on Git checkouts.
  - Removed failing `PostBuildEvent` (`xcopy` to hardcoded `C:\Buddy\Projects\...`).
* **AutoEquip Conflict Resolution ([AutoAngler.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/AutoAngler.cs))**:
  - Honorbuddy's built-in AutoEquip engine scored equipped fishing poles as 0.18 and continuously re-equipped the player's weapon in combat/fishing bags, triggering an infinite weapon swap loop.
  - Added automatic suppression in `Start()`: stores original `CharacterSettings.Instance.AutoEquipWeapons` state and temporarily disables it, plus dynamically discovers and temporarily disables any loaded `AutoEquip` plugins via `PluginManager.Plugins`.
  - In `Stop()`: safely restores `CharacterSettings.Instance.AutoEquipWeapons` and re-enables all suppressed plugins.
* **Equip Pole Throttling & Null-Safety ([EquipPoleAction.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/Composites/EquipPoleAction.cs))**:
  - Added a 1.5-second equip throttle timer to eliminate frame-by-frame Lua `EquipItemByName` spam while waiting for the server/client equip animation to complete.
  - Added null checks for `ItemInfo` when querying equipped items and bag items.
* **Weapon Equip Crash Fix ([Util.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/Util.cs))**:
  - In `Utils.EquipWeapon()`, guarded `weapon != null && weapon.ItemInfo != null` before accessing `weapon.ItemInfo.InventoryType`, preventing runtime `NullReferenceException` if the configured weapon is missing or being moved.
* **Fishing Bobber Detection & Use ([FishAction.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/Composites/FishAction.cs))**:
  - Replaced `o.CreatedBy.Guid == Me.Guid` (which threw `NullReferenceException` on non-unit creators, swallowed in an empty catch block) with direct and fast memory-backed `o.CreatedByGuid == Me.Guid`.
  - Safely cast `bobber.SubObj as WoWFishingBobber` before accessing `.IsBobbing` and `.Use()` to prevent `InvalidCastException`.
* **Path Generation Safety ([MoveToPoolAction.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/Composites/MoveToPoolAction.cs))**:
  - Added null check `testP != null && testP.Length > 0` on `Navigator.GeneratePath()` results.
* **Loot Collection Null Guards ([LootAction.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/Composites/LootAction.cs), [LootNPCsAction.cs](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Bots/AutoAngler2/Composites/LootNPCsAction.cs))**:
  - Changed `FishCaught` setter from `private set` to `internal set` in `AutoAnglerBot` so composites can ensure initialization without throwing.
  - Added defensive guards for `lootInfo != null && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(lootInfo.LootName)`.
* **Compilation Status**: Verified 0 errors and 0 build failures with Microsoft C# 5.0 compiler targeting .NET 4.5.1 x86 in both Debug and Release configurations.

