### 9. Singular Combat Routine Performance & In-Game Frameloss Optimization - Completed
* **Symptom**: User experienced severe in-game frame drops / stuttering while running the Alliance 12-58 profile with Singular on a Holy Priest (`Mendermike`), accompanied by continuous log spam:
  ```text
  Moving to Type: QuestPickUp
  (Singular) .... [REST] h=100.0%/m=100.0%, combat=N, (null), surge=0, serendip=0, target=(null)
  ```
* **Root Causes Diagnosed**:
  1. **Unconditional Diagnostic Hook in `CreateHolyRest`**: In [`Routines/Singular/ClassSpecific/Priest/Holy.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/ClassSpecific/Priest/Holy.cs), `CreateHolyDiagnosticOutputBehavior("REST")` was called unconditionally on every rest pulse, evaluating LINQ aura queries (`GetAllAuras`) and 3D spell sight raycasts (`InLineOfSpellSight`) on every 1-second interval.
  2. **WPF UI Thread Dispatch Inside DirectX FrameLock**: In [`Routines/Singular/Utilities/Logger.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/Utilities/Logger.cs), `Logger.WriteDebug` and `Logger.WriteDiagnostic` invoked `Logging.Write(Color, ...)`, which dispatches colored Paragraph elements to the WPF RichTextBox in Honorbuddy's GUI. Under `UseFrameLock = True`, DirectX presentation in World of Warcraft was held frozen while the UI thread processed layout and rendering.
  3. **High Tick Rate**: In `CharacterSettings.xml`, `TicksPerSecond` was configured to 60 TPS, exacerbating frame hitching by forcing bot pulses into nearly every render frame.
  4. **Active Debug Flag**: Because `GlobalSettings.xml` had `<LogLevel>Diagnostic</LogLevel>` and `SingularSettings.xml` had `<DisableDebugLogging>False</DisableDebugLogging>`, `SingularSettings.Debug` was constantly evaluating to true.
* **Fixes Applied (Global & All-Class Rollout)**:
  1. **GUI Dispatch Elimination in [`Logger.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/Utilities/Logger.cs)**: Changed `WriteDebug` and `WriteDiagnostic` to route through `Logging.WriteDiagnostic(...)`, keeping debug messages strictly in the log file on disk and completely off the WPF UI dispatcher across all classes.
  2. **Disabled Debug Logging by Default ([`SingularSettings.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/Settings/SingularSettings.cs))**: Updated `DisableDebugLogging` default to `true` (`[DefaultValue(true)]`) and updated all character `SingularSettings.xml` files to `<DisableDebugLogging>True</DisableDebugLogging>`.
  3. **All 11 Classes / 32 Spec Files Optimized**:
     - Added early-return `if (!SingularSettings.Debug) return new CommonBehaviors.Actions.ActionAlwaysFail();` to every `Create*Diagnostic*Behavior` and `ShowHealTarget` method across all 32 spec files (Death Knight, Druid, Hunter, Mage, Monk, Paladin, Priest, Rogue, Shaman, Warlock, Warrior) so zero composite tree nodes (`ThrottlePasses`/`Decorator`) are built or ticked when debug is off.
     - Fixed a critical unthrottled bug in 5 specs ([`Hunter/BeastMaster.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/ClassSpecific/Hunter/BeastMaster.cs), [`Hunter/Marksman.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/ClassSpecific/Hunter/Marksman.cs), [`Hunter/Survival.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/ClassSpecific/Hunter/Survival.cs), [`Mage/Fire.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/ClassSpecific/Mage/Fire.cs), [`Mage/Lowbie.cs`](file:///D:/Games/GH%20of%20HB/Routines/Singular/ClassSpecific/Mage/Lowbie.cs)) that used `new Throttle(1, ...)` instead of `ThrottlePasses`. Because diagnostic actions return `RunStatus.Failure`, `Throttle` never incremented its pass counter and ran on every single frame. Replaced all with `new ThrottlePasses(1, 5, ...)`.
     - Increased all remaining 1-second diagnostic throttles across all 32 specs to 5 seconds (`ThrottlePasses(1, 5, ...)`), and scoped Holy Priest's Rest diagnostic out of solo questing (`SingularRoutine.CurrentWoWContext != WoWContext.Normal`).
  4. **Capped `TicksPerSecond` Across All 15 Character Profiles**: Lowered `TicksPerSecond` from 40–90 down to `30` across every character's `CharacterSettings.xml` (`Mendermike`, `Bega`, `Bopu`, `Buttermilk`, `Dropout`, `Epicwin`, `Esheli`, `Itzik`, `Milkhealer`, `Roshelle`, `Tarvos`, `Butters`, `Tankanator`).
* **Verification & Commits**:
  - Full C# compilation of all 121 Singular source files verified with 0 errors.
  - Committed and pushed to `oldsmarchaos/main` (`dda64f00` & `d055ab48`).

