* **HB Core Fix: `FlightPaths` Sanitizer (`Plugins/FixFlightPathMoveTo/FixFlightPathMoveTo.cs`, v2.0.0.0)** (`cd277545` .. `a755d6dc`):
  - **Incident**: `Styx.CommonBot.FlightPaths.smethod_0` (RVA `0xd86a8`) threw `InvalidOperationException: Sequence contains no matching element` inside `MeshNavigator.MoveTo` -> `FlightPaths.ShouldTakeFlightpath` when questing in Searing Gorge / Burning Steppes.
  - **Root Cause #1 (`FlightPaths.smethod_4` / `smethod_0`)**: When `TAXIMAP_OPENED` fires (`smethod_4` @ RVA `0xd884c`), HB iterates all DBC taxi nodes and adds every node to `FlightPaths.XmlNodes` (and `Settings\<Realm>\<Char>\FlightPaths.xml`), even when `!taxiFrameNode.Reachable`. This polluted `FlightPaths.XmlNodes` with 50+ unreachable, opposite-faction, and debug DBC nodes with empty `<Connections />` (such as `"Generic, World Target 002"` at `-6666, -2222.3, 278.6`). When the player was closer to one of those unconnected nodes than to a real flight master, `smethod_0` selected it as `xmlFlightNode_2` and called `Enumerable.First(n => list_0.Contains(n.Name))` (`IL_00af`) on an empty connections list.
  - **Root Cause #2 (`Navigator.set_NavigationProvider` Disposing `MeshNavigator`)**: Decompiling `Styx.Pathing.Navigator` and `Styx.Pathing.MeshNavigator` revealed that replacing `Navigator.NavigationProvider` with a non-`MeshNavigator` wrapper causes `Navigator.set_NavigationProvider` to invoke `MeshNavigator.OnRemoveAsCurrent()`, which unhooks `BotEvents.OnPulse` (`UpdateMaps()`) and calls `Nav.Dispose()` (`Nav.Mesh = null`, `Nav.MeshQuery = null`), causing `WowNavigator.FindPath` to throw `NullReferenceException` on `MeshQuery.FindNearestPolygon`.
  - **Fix (`a755d6dc`)**: Removed the `INavigationProvider` wrapper so `MeshNavigator` and `WowNavigator` remain 100% native and untouched (and automatically restores a fresh `MeshNavigator` if hot-reloaded over an older wrapped session). Directly sanitizes `FlightPaths.XmlNodes` and saves the cleaned `FlightPaths.xml` by removing bogus `MasterEntry == 0` nodes with empty `<Connections />` / `WoWPoint.Empty` and ignoring any isolated node locations via `FlightPaths.IgnoreFp(node.Location)` to a fixed point, guaranteeing every active candidate in `FlightPaths.smethod_0` has a valid connected destination on the same continent.

* **MrPlow AddOn Coroutine Boundary & Options Sync (Interface/AddOns/MrPlow/)**:
  - **Incident**: Running MrPlow threw ttempt to yield across metamethod/C-call boundary at MrPlow\PlowEngine.lua:807 (coroutine.yield(self) inside MassSort) called from PlowScheduler.OnUpdate (PlowEngine.lua:915).
  - **Root Cause**: PlowScheduler.OnUpdate (a C-to-Lua OnUpdate handler running on the main thread) invoked 
extCall[1](...) directly as a normal function call instead of wrapping it in the sortbags coroutine (coroutine.create). Whenever a bag slot was still locked from the preceding Restack/Defragment job (select(3, infoFunc(bag, slot)) == true), MassSort (or Restack) executed coroutine.yield(self) across the C OnUpdate boundary.
  - **Fix**: Wrapped initial job dispatch in PlowScheduler.OnUpdate inside sortbags = coroutine.create(...) with protected coroutine.resume, added slot-lock yielding and state persistence to Consolidate and Defragment, fixed numeric vs. string IgnoreItems / SortItemID lookups, guarded ReverseProcessBags and CanGoInBag against nil arguments, and synced the complete MrPlow addon (including PlowOptions.lua GUI and embedded Ace3 libraries) between D:\Games\TwinStar WoW\Interface\AddOns\MrPlow and Interface/AddOns/MrPlow/.

